    rdf:value "- FSA A.6 03.058, on which Joseph Upton's classification mentions \"N-58\", provides Ernst Herzfeld's personal diary for the year 1931. The earliest registered entry dates, \"Jan. 15, 1931\", and the latest registered entry dates, \"Nov. 27, 1931." .

kg:note_ref8266_scopecontent_1_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdf:value "- Additional information from staff reads: \"At the end of the diary, Herzfeld has several annotations including a transcription of a cuneiform inscription found on Luristan bronze daggers, a Greek inscription on a stone tablet from Susa, and two Arabic inscriptions, in Kufic script, from the Tachara Palace (Palace of Darius) in Persepolis (Iran).\"" .

