    crm:P3_has_note "Arrangement In the original arrangement of the Ernst Herzfeld Archive, Notebooks were included in a larger body of diverse material acknowledged by Ernst Herzfeld as his study collection. In the early 1970s, Joseph Upton, for research purpose, rearranged the collection and created a specific series (Ernst Herzfeld Papers, Series 3: Notebooks, 1904-1946, 1957, n.d.) for 131 notebooks, including four ledgers and eight travel journals. Upton has given this notebook an accession number, N-37, related to the series he created for the notebooks, probably following Herzfeld's original organization.",
        "General - Title is provided by Xavier Courouble, FSg Archives cataloger, based on Joseph Upton's Catalogue of the Herzfeld Archive.",
        "Local Numbers Ernst Herzfeld Papers; N-37 FSA A.6 03.037",
        "Scope and Contents - Handwritten caption, in pencil (probably by Joseph Upton), on front cover reads: \"B.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-37, p. 1 reads, \"Bronze axe-head, Harsin. Tehran Museum.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-37, p. 14 reads, \"Itinerary Kazerun-Dar Ahani via Bahrām II relief near Nurabad.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-37, p. 15 reads, \"Quotation from letter from Enno Littman on 'Adud al-daula inscription of 363 H..\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-37, p. 16 reads, \"List of purchases in Hamadan.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-37, p. 17 reads, \"Seal from Nihāvand vase with cuneiform inscription.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-37, p. 2 reads, \"Notes on Luristan bronze daggers with cuneiform inscriptions.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-37, p. 20 reads, \"Notes on prehistoric seals in British Museum.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-37, p. 21 reads, \"Cuneiform inscription on Luristan bronze vessel.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-37, p. 22 reads, \"Sasanian seal with Pahlavi inscription, Munich.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-37, p. 23 reads, \"Early bronze picks and pins from various sites.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-37, p. 24 reads, \"Early bronze rings, pendants, etc. from various sites.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-37, p. 25 reads, \"Prehistoric seals and bracelet. Constantinople and Damascus.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-37, p. 28 reads, \"Arabic inscription on E door of city-gate. Constantinople (?).\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-37, p. 29 reads, \"Tabula ansata in Damascus Museum, 456 H..\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-37, p. 3 reads, \"Greek inscription on stone tablet, Susa.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-37, p. 4 reads, \"Apparently a quotation from a Greek elegy on the Parthians.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-37, p. 5 reads, \"Inscription on silver, bronze inlaid candlestick.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-37, p. 6 reads, \"Arabic inscription on Herzfeld's pen-box.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-37, p. 7 reads, \"Bronze kettle with cuneiform inscription.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-37, pp. 10 and 11 reads, \"(a) Sasanian bulla with inscription, Tehran Museum (b) Arabic inscription on wooden door, Abadeh.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-37, pp. 12 and 13 reads, \"Arabic inscription of 520 H. on wooden door, Abadeh.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-37, pp. 18 and 19 reads, \"Cuneiform inscription of Artaxerxes on silver plate from Hamadan.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-37, pp. 26 and 27 reads, \"Stone basin in Constantinople and notes on objects there.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-37, pp. 30 to 32 reads, \"Arabic inscriptions, Damascus Museum. Noted Aug./Sept. 1941.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-37, pp. 8 and 9 reads, \"Isfahān, Masjid-i Jum'a. Arabic inscriptions in dome chambers.\"" ;
