    crm:P3_has_note "Arrangement In the original arrangement of the Ernst Herzfeld Archive, Notebooks were included in a larger body of diverse material acknowledged by Ernst Herzfeld as his study collection. In the early 1970s, Joseph Upton, for research purpose, rearranged the collection and created a specific series (Ernst Herzfeld Papers, Series 3: Notebooks, 1904-1946, 1957, n.d.) for 131 notebooks, including four ledgers and eight travel journals. Upton has given this notebook an accession number, N-39, related to the series he created for the notebooks, probably following Herzfeld's original organization.",
        "General - Title is provided by Xavier Courouble, FSg Archives cataloger, based on Joseph Upton's Catalogue of the Herzfeld Archive.",
        "Local Numbers Ernst Herzfeld Papers; N-39 FSA A.6 03.039",
        "Scope and Contents - FSA A.6 03.039, on which Joseph Upton's classification mentions \"N-39\", provides ten water-colors of various sites in Iran. The late Karl Bergner was a highly gifted architectural draftsman who worked for Professor Herzfeld at Persepolis and subsequently for Dr. Erich Schmidt at Istakhr. He usually took a trip during his vacation. On one such trip in 1935 he painted these water-colors for his own pleasure.",
        "Scope and Contents - Handwritten caption, in pencil (probably by Joseph Upton), on front cover reads: \"Sketchbook Bergner.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-39, p. 1 reads, \"Persepolis column and plain, Oct. 6, 1935.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-39, p. 10 reads, \"Left side of Taq-i Kisra, Ctesiphon (Iraq).\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-39, p. 2 reads, \"Kumishah, mosque.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-39, p. 3 reads, \"Mahun (shrine), March 3, 1935.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-39, p. 4 reads, \"Ice-houses in Kerman, April 3, 1935.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-39, p. 5 reads, \"Tulip and pansy.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-39, p. 6 reads, \"Masjid-i Jum'a near Kerman, April 3, 1935.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-39, p. 7 reads, \"Unfinished tomb of Kambyses near Persepolis, April 28, 1935.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-39, p. 8 reads, \"Ruins of a garden house two Km W. of Persepolis, July 5, 1935.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-39, p. 9 reads, \"Beginnings of a pencil sketch.\"" ;
