        kg:concept_aat_300264354 ;
    crm:P3_has_note "Arrangement In the original arrangement of the Ernst Herzfeld Archive, Notebooks were included in a larger body of diverse material acknowledged by Ernst Herzfeld as his study collection. In the early 1970s, Joseph Upton, for research purpose, rearranged the collection and created a specific series (Ernst Herzfeld Papers, Series 3: Notebooks, 1904-1946, 1957, n.d.) for 131 notebooks, including four ledgers and eight travel journals. Upton has given this notebook an accession number, N-125, related to the series he created for the notebooks, probably following Herzfeld's original organization.",
        "General - Title is provided by Xavier Courouble, FSg Archives cataloger, based on Joseph Upton's Catalogue of the Herzfeld Archive.",
        "Local Numbers Ernst Herzfeld Papers; N-125 FSA A.6 03.125",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-125, folder 1 reads, \"\"Damascus: Studies in Architecture-II\" (Ars Islamica) page proofs of text.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-125, folder 10 reads, \"Pencil sketches of three bridges near Khurramabad and letter, Feb.2, 1926.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-125, folder 11 reads, \"Notes and copies of Arabic inscriptions in Great Mosque, Hamah and in Damascus.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-125, folder 12 reads, \"Photostat copy of \"An Achaemenian tomb-inscription at Persepolis,\" Davis. JRAS, April, 1932.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-125, folder 13 reads, \"Newspaper clipping from Dichtung und Welt (Prague) No.40, 1929. \"Arkona und Rethra.\" Eine Glosse zu Strzygowskis Werk, \"Altslaview Kunst.\" J. Peisker.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-125, folder 14 reads, \"First version of \"Damascus: Studies in Architecture IV\" (final version published in Ars Islamica).\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-125, folder 15 reads, \"Notes on Hebrew inscriptions in synagogue, Aleppo.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-125, folder 16 reads, \"Notes on bronze object with cuneiform inscription AMI, vol.IX, pp.159-177 (see Photo File 6-18/22).\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-125, folder 17 reads, \"Six offprints of \"Damascus: Studies in Architecture-IV\".\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-125, folder 2 reads, \"\"Damascus: Studies in Architecture-I\" (Ars Islamica) page proofs of illustrations.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-125, folder 3 reads, \"\"Simplified Outline of Sanskrit Historical Phonology...,'\" F.Edgerton.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-125, folder 4 reads, \"Notebook of rough sketches and descriptions of 74 objects (perhaps for unidentified loan).\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-125, folder 5 reads, \"List of Persepolis Expedition field negatives with numbers of corresponding Oriental Institute catalogue numbers.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-125, folder 6 reads, \"Herzfeld's undated proposal for publication of 22 volumes over a 10-year period, covering his life work to about 1932.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-125, folder 7 reads, \"Letter of April 19, 1934 from N.L.Falcon enclosing photo of \"boulder\" (astodān?) in Tang Malagha with map of location.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-125, folder 8 reads, \"Notes and sketches of rock-tombs in Paphlagonia.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-125, folder 9 reads, \"Note on ruins at Holilan (near Kermanshah) and sketch of Luristan bronze.\"" ;
