    rdf:value "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, Joseph Upton's caption for N-32 reads, \"Contains draft outline of chapter headings and sub-headings for The Persian Empire, with identification of 17 proposed illustrations. See N-120/121 for Ms. edited and published posthumously by Prof. Gerold Walser, 1968. The first chapter, \"The Horse in the Ancient East...,\" bears a notation \"Verőffentl. d. Türk. Geschichts Kommission, V. Serie. No.2a. Ausgrabungen von Alaca Hőyük von Dr. Hēmit Zübeyr KoÅŸay (Ankara, 1944). Der Gold-eisen dolch (?) in dem darauf folgenden Nummern.\" The notebook also contains miscellaneous notes related to the study.\"" ;
    mbs:noteType mbs:ScopeContent .

